// Fixture (expected-NOT-noop, safety-critical case): inherits both
// branches of a STATEFUL diamond. dvar is duplicated (once via each
// path), so this object's total variable count is DOUBLE the base's --
// must NOT be treated as a no-op (the num_variables_total equality
// check must catch the mismatch).
//
// Deliberately defines nothing of its own beyond create(): try_bind()
// comes from replace_diamond_var_x.lpc (previously defined locally here,
// which masked the discriminator this fixture claims to isolate -- with
// a local try_bind(), the check would correctly refuse regardless of
// whether the variable-count equality logic worked). var_offset still
// resolves to 0 here (search_inherited finds x through the first branch,
// replace_diamond_var_a), so the num_variables_total equality check
// really is the sole remaining guard.
inherit "/clone/replace_program/replace_diamond_var_a";
inherit "/clone/replace_program/replace_diamond_var_b";
void create() { replace_program("/clone/replace_program/replace_diamond_var_x"); }
